.TH TENSOR-GPU-LIFECYCLE-GUARD 1 "2026-11-24" "Tensor infrastructure" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
 tensor-gpu-lifecycle-guard \- read-only wallpaper start policy and owner identity checks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 shared/scripts/tensor-gpu-lifecycle-guard.py
.RI [ --db " PATH" ]
.RI [ --check-wallpaper-start ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stage 2D safety predicate. Reads the existing GPU lease database without mutation.
Refuses wallpaper startup candidates during preparing, reserved, or restore_pending states.
The optional check flag exits 1 when state cannot be verified or a lease is active.
The Python module also provides a Linux PID+starttime+boot ID identity classifier.
Neither the CLI nor this module modifies services, performs recovery, or unloads GPU models.
.PP
.B WARNING:
This predicate alone is not an atomic systemd start guard, and is not installed
as a service hook in Stage 2D. Race-safe wallpaper startup and owner registration
are required before enabling a real lease coordinator.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/state/tensor-gpu-lease/queue.sqlite3
is the proposed protected runtime state (not created by the guard).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tensor-gpu-lease (1),
.BR tensor-gpu-systemd-adapter (1).
